(vector 
 (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "2607182500")
  (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-8291: IPNS graph publication to kotobase.net via kotobase-llm")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/decided "2026-07-18")
  (:adr/body "## Summary

Formalize IPNS graph publication for cloud-itonami-isic-8291 actor:
- **Source**: Actor's CACAO did:key (self-generated, no server custody)
- **Destination**: IPNS graph rooted at `k51qzi5uqu5d...` (derived from did:key)
- **Orchestration**: cloud-itonami-lei-update-routine invokes kotobase-llm for publish
- **Discovery**: Graph registered in kotobase.net discovery surface (`.well-known/did.json` + web)
- **Benefit**: LEI repo metadata + governance attestations discoverable via IPNS

## Design

### 1. Actor Identity (ADR-2607182300 baseline)

```edn
{:actor/id \"cloud-itonami-isic-8291\"
 :actor/did-key \"did:key:z6MkoVNKPFF9pJu8jGjvTqm7HJu89mGANsdeMWC61ob3R8K3\"
 :actor/ipns-name \"k51qzi5uqu5djj242v98agipmdsetwgdv49t19eijjewkykbcze2q5demc7gky\"
 :actor/identity-journal \"80-data/kotoba-rad/cloud-itonami-isic-8291.identity.journal.edn\"}
```

Identity sealed in `.dossier/identity.edn` (local, gitignored).

### 2. Graph Structure

IPNS graph at `k51qzi5uqu5d...` contains:

```edn
{:graph/type :actor-discovery
 :graph/actor-id \"cloud-itonami-isic-8291\"
 :graph/did-key \"did:key:z6Mk...\"
 :graph/lei-repos
 [{:repo-name \"cloud-itonami-lei-j3whbg0mts7o8zvmdc91\"
   :lei \"J3WHBG0MTS7O8ZVMDC91\"
   :company \"Exxon Mobil Corporation\"
   :github-url \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-lei-j3whbg0mts7o8zvmdc91\"
   :tos-doc-count 1
   :published-at \"2026-07-18T18:00:00Z\"}
  ;; ... 108 more repos
  ]
 :graph/governance
 {:proposer-role \"Advisor-LLM (Dossier-LLM)\"
  :approver-roles [\"6-stage-Governor\" \"DisclosureGovernor\"]
  :ledger-path \"manifest/fleet-db.ledger.edn\"
  :last-update \"2026-07-18T18:30:00Z\"}
 :graph/metadata
 {:version \"1.0\"
  :schema \"actor-discovery-graph-v1\"
  :signature {:algorithm \"Ed25519\"
              :public-key \"z6MkoVNKPFF9pJu8jGjvTqm7HJu89mGANsdeMWC61ob3R8K3\"
              :signature \"<base64-signature>\"}}}
### 3. Orchestration (via bin/collect-routine.clj)

After successful LEI collection:

```clj
(publish-ipns
  {:did-key actor-identity
   :ipns-name ipns-root
   :graph-data {:lei-repos discovered-repos
                :governance {:last-update timestamp}}
   :signature {:algorithm \"Ed25519\"
               :key (:private-key actor-identity)}})
```

Steps:
1. Serialize graph to EDN + sign with actor's private key
2. Invoke `kotobase-llm` cell (murakumo-supplied) with graph + signature
3. kotobase-llm publishes to IPNS via embedded go-ipfs
4. Return root hash + timestamp
5. Append to `fleet-db.ledger.edn` for audit trail

### 4. Discovery Registration

kotobase.net discovery surface (`.well-known/did.json`):

```json
{
  \"@context\": [\"https://www.w3.org/ns/did/v1\"],
  \"id\": \"did:key:z6MkoVNK...\",
  \"service\": [
    {
      \"id\": \"#lei-discovery\",
      \"type\": \"IpfsGraph\",
      \"serviceEndpoint\": \"ipns://k51qzi5uqu5d...\",
      \"description\": \"cloud-itonami-isic-8291 LEI repository graph\"
    }
  ]
}
```

Consumers can resolve:
- Web: `https://kotobase.net/.well-known/did.json?did=did:key:z6Mk...`
- IPNS: `ipns://k51qzi5uqu5d...` (via kubo / js-ipfs)

## Scope & Limitations

### Scope
- **Publish on each LEI collection tick** (hourly)
- **Graph versioned** by timestamp + signature chain (immutable)
- **No server custody** — actor holds its own private key, signs its own graph

### Honest Limitations
- **kotobase-server dependency**: Cannot publish without kotobase-llm cell availability
- **IPNS replication lag**: Nodes may take minutes to see new hash (IPFS/IPNS propagation latency)
- **Data freshness trade-off**: Hourly ticks vs. immediate client reads (clients see eventual consistency)

## Verification

- **Unit test**: Verify signature round-trip (sign → serialize → verify)
- **E2E dry-run**: `--dry-run` mode generates graph JSON (no actual publish)
- **Live test**: Deploy to murakumo with short lease; verify graph appears at IPNS hash within 5 min
- **Consumer test**: Fetch via `ipfs cat /ipns/k51qzi5uqu5d.../` and verify structure + signature

## Sequence

1. **[Current]** ADR approval (this record)
2. **[Next iteration]** Implement kotobase-llm integration in `bin/collect-routine.clj`
   - Add `publish-ipns` fn body (currently stub)
   - Wire up actor identity → signature
   - Invoke murakumo cell
3. **[Next iteration]** Test locally (dry-run) + on murakumo (live)
4. **[Deploy]** Integrate into `cloud-itonami-lei-update-hourly` routine

## Related

- **ADR-2607182300** — Actor identity + CACAO self-mint (prerequisite)
- **ADR-2607182400** — Murakumo routine orchestration (calls this publish step)
- **ADR-2607110300** — LEI collection baseline (D6 forward reference, now being fulfilled)
- **ADR-2605192100** — Charter (Actor autonomy, no server-side signing, IPNS as authority)
- **ADR-2606111400** — Member CACAO leash (actor's CACAO revocation path, if needed)

## Success Criteria

- ✅ Actor's private key never transmitted to server (sealed locally)
- ✅ Graph published to IPNS on each successful collection tick
- ✅ Signature verifiable by consumers
- ✅ `.well-known/did.json` discoverable and accurate
- ✅ IPNS graph contents reflect current LEI repo inventory
- ✅ Ledger records every publish attempt (success + failure)

## Notes

This fulfills ADR-2607110300's forward reference (\"kotobase.net ingestion\"). The actor now has a publishable identity rooted on blockchain-accessible IPNS, enabling decentralized discovery and attestation of its governance decisions.

Post-publication, LEI repo consumers (downstream actors, CI/CD agents, humans) can fetch the graph from IPNS, verify the signature, and trust the LEI metadata as coming from the actor itself — not from a central server.")
